  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340682",
      "title": "Navigating Programmatically",
      "lectureOrder": 151,
      "videoOrder": 140,
      "sourceHash": "8c3a3a5a47529c9d63fa0c803c0f86f3baab754844241235ec75e27e3163c8e8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.05,
          "end": 3.45,
          "en": "Now, of course here, it would be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.45,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "if we could click on this backdrop and then go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 10.29,
          "en": "to that detail page where we're coming from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.29,
          "end": 13.02,
          "en": "and we can implement this feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.02,
          "end": 17.61,
          "en": "by adding a click listener on this modal backdrop div,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.61,
          "end": 21.3,
          "en": "and by then triggering some code that does take us back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.3,
          "end": 23.7,
          "en": "to the page we're coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.7,
          "end": 28.11,
          "en": "So what we want to do here is navigate programmatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.11,
          "end": 28.943,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.943,
          "end": 32.7,
          "en": "We wanna trigger a navigation from inside our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.7,
          "end": 35.548,
          "en": "so not because the user clicked a link or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.548,
          "end": 39.96,
          "en": "because the user manually clicked the back button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.96,
          "end": 42.27,
          "en": "but instead from inside our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.27,
          "end": 44.703,
          "en": "because the user clicked this div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.96,
          "end": 48.96,
          "en": "And to navigate programmatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.96,
          "end": 52.98,
          "en": "NextJS gives you the special use router hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.98,
          "end": 56.85,
          "en": "which must be imported from next slash navigation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.85,
          "end": 61.083,
          "en": "not from some other package, but from next slash navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.07,
          "end": 65.55,
          "en": "This gives you access to a router object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.55,
          "end": 67.74,
          "en": "which then holds various methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.74,
          "end": 70.113,
          "en": "for navigating around programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.98,
          "end": 73.5,
          "en": "For example, you can call the push method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 78.42,
          "en": "to push a new page onto the stack of pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.42,
          "end": 82.68,
          "en": "You can also manually refresh the page by calling refresh,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 86.28,
          "en": "but now it's actually this back method I'm interested in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.28,
          "end": 90.3,
          "en": "because if you call that, the user is navigated back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.3,
          "end": 92.07300000000001,
          "en": "to the page they're coming from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "and that's what I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 96.96000000000001,
          "en": "to do when the user clicks this backdrop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.96000000000001,
          "end": 99.66,
          "en": "Therefore, here as a value for on click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.66,
          "end": 102.96000000000001,
          "en": "I'll register this router back method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.96000000000001,
          "end": 105.18,
          "en": "I'm not executing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.18,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "so you should not add these parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108,
          "end": 110.88,
          "en": "Instead, we just point at this method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.88,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "and it will therefore be executed for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 116.283,
          "en": "whenever a click on this div occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.12,
          "end": 119.85,
          "en": "Now, this use router hook, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.85,
          "end": 122.82,
          "en": "only works inside of client components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.82,
          "end": 125.91,
          "en": "Therefore, we must now actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.91,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "add this use client directive to the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 130.773,
          "en": "of this file to make it work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.15,
          "end": 134.82,
          "en": "But with that, if you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.82,
          "end": 137.4,
          "en": "you of course are on the full screen details page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.4,
          "end": 142.02,
          "en": "but if you go there by clicking around, this modal opens up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.02,
          "end": 144.36,
          "en": "and if you then click on the background here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.36,
          "end": 146.64,
          "en": "you see it closes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.64,
          "end": 149.73,
          "en": "But essentially that means that we are navigated back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.73,
          "end": 151.47,
          "en": "to the path we're coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.47,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "You can also see how the path changes up here when I click",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 157.23,
          "en": "on the backdrop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.23,
          "end": 160.263,
          "en": "And that's how you can navigate around programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
